Capture the Windows error at the point of failure in SpawnTarget.

FinishSpawnTargetImpl called GetLastError after ApplyToTarget had returned, by
which time the target had been destroyed and terminated. So for most failures
the reported error was stale or unrelated, and for failures that are not caused
by a Windows API call it was meaningless.

Pass last_error into ApplyToTarget and on to TargetProcess::Init,
TransferVariable and VerifySentinels, so that it is set straight after the
failing call and is ERROR_SUCCESS for failures that are just logic checks.
Also return the error from DropActiveProcessLimit.

SetupAllInterceptions and SetupHandleCloser have many internal failure points,
so rather than pass last_error through all of them, the last error is cleared
before calling them and read afterwards.

